{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792796-christmas-present-for-kinda-everyone-3e-solar-brawl-punch-charms","id":792796,"title":"Christmas Present for kinda everyone [3e Solar Brawl punch charms]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-25T12:19:40-08:00","id":792796,"title":"Christmas Present for kinda everyone [3e Solar Brawl punch charms]","content":"So I forgot we were doing a white elephant this year on the boards, probably because doing my job made me forget largely everything else. So in honour of that, and since I have no way of finishing Infernals in a single day, I decided to do something quick and easy. That is the 2.5e Ink Monkey charms translated into 3e focused around punching people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Sandact, we already have charms to punch people really ha- </div> </div> </div>THOSE ARE NOT PUNCHING HARD ENOUGH! YOU NEED TO PUNCH UNTIL THE SKY SPLITS OPEN BECAUSE THE CLOUDS ARE SAYING &quot;GET IN THE WAY OF THAT? FUCK THAT&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>HELLRAISER\u2019S INSTINCT</b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: - (5m)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 2\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Sledgehammer Fist Punch<br /> <br /> This Charm allows the Lawgiver to deliver an ironic comeuppance to his enemy or dramatic landscape rearrangement. Whenever the Solar uses a throw to ram his opponent into scenery, or a Charm which causes such an impact directly (such as Heaven Thunder Hammer or the smashing tag), he may pay six motes to trigger this Charm\u2019s effects:<br /> <br /> When the opponent impacts with a solid surface, the impact causes extreme damage to the structure in question. To determine how much damage is done, use the Lawgiver\u2019s ratings to roll a (Strength + Brawl + Essence) dice attack against the structure in question. Treat this attack as one being enhanced by Sledgehammer Fist Punch, adding Strength Automatic successes to the attempt. At Essence +4, add an amount of successes equal to the falling damage such a victim would tag to the surface instead.<br /> <br /> When the target takes health levels of damage from such an impact, the Exalt\u2019s player may choose to defer a number of health levels from the victim and transfer them into the structure his victim has impacted with. Each health level deferred in this way translates into +2 effective strength in determining the amount of strength needed whenever the exalt can break the object or not (This does not add dice, just increases effective strength rating). If the damage would have been sufficient to knock out or kill the opponent and the damage roll had seven or more successes on it (the decisive damage roll, not the falling damage), than mundane structures take enough damage to be sufficiently destroyed immediately. In the case of very large structures such as mountains, you blow out a very sizable portion instead. At Essence 5 if the Solar also knows Nine Aeons Thew, then when activated along with this charm it allows him to literally shatter mountains in a single punch. Or if you want to do the ESS 5 effect immediately, go ahead I don\u2019t care.<br /> <br /> If the opponent takes any health level damage upon the attack, they take a penalty equal to their current onslaught penalty that lasts until the end of their next turn. In addition they need to roll Dexterity+Athletics or Stamina + Resistance to stand up at a difficulty of 3, dazed from the impact of the strike.<br /> <br /> This charm is fueled by the Exalt\u2019s killing intent, they cannot use it to throw rats into mountains causing them to explode... unless the rat was a hated rat totem lunar.<br /> <br /> <b>BREAK THROUGH THE WORLD</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>\u200b: - (+7m 1WP)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Sledgehammer Fist Punch<br /> <br /> <i>DEATH</i><br /> <br /> The loftiest works of men, gods, and Primordials alike are as dust before the fury of the Solar Exalted. This charm supplements a Feat of Strength to break something with the exalts bare hands or with Hellraiser\u2019s Instinct. It allows the Exalt to use Strength+Brawl instead of Strength+Athletics on the roll if it didn\u2019t already. Additionally if the feat of the strength is successful, then the Exalt\u2019s wrath knocks far more out than just a single lock or door. Entire trees can be blown into splinters while even lofty castles can have entire sections outright vaporized at once. If the Exalts Feat of Strength roll is enough to break everything out to a range of medium (or Essence x10 meters if you wish to use that) than all of those objects are immediately destroyed by the blast of air pressure that goes along with it. At Essence 5 for +10m 1WP the Exalt may encompass an area up to long range (or Essence x50 meters if that is preferred). At Essence 6 this may be applied to non-perishable magical items and structures.<br /> <br /> <b>MOUNTAIN OBLITERATION TEMPEST</b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: - (+3m or 1HL of damage)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Break Through the World<br /> <br /> The Solars blows are enough to tear apart mountains, an angry tempest from myth and legend that all rightfully fear. This charm upgrades Break Through the World, in which if the target impacts a surface and the damage is enough to destroy the object, the exalt may pay 3m or do one less level of impact damage, after which the object the person collided with is destroyed and they continue to fly in a straight line until they hit another object, after which this charm may be activated again until no impact levels of damage are left or the opponent\u2019s travel distance is completed. Hellraiser\u2019s Instinct is applied to all feat of strength rolls to see if the exalt can break something for free, allowing each person hit with this charm to dig massive trenches or gouges in the earth from the sheer force of the blow.<br /> <br /> At Essence 5, any feat of Strength charm and Break Through the World only need to be paid for once and their effects may be reapplied for as many objects in the way of the punch. This means if an Exalt is on top of a skyscraper the can punch someone straight down and possibly obliterate half of the entire building in the process.<br /> <br /> <b>METEOR IMPACT SMASH</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>\u200b: - (+5m)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords\u200b</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms\u200b</b>: Heaven Thunder Hammer OR Crashing Wave Throw<br /> <br /> <i>TELL THAT TO THE METEOR IDIOT!</i><br /> <br /> The impacts of the Solar hero are like meteors of rage being cast down to earth itself, annihilating all in their path. This charm functions as an upgrade to its prerequisites, enhancing them whenever their opponent suffers damage as if being hit from a medium distance impact or if they\u2019re somehow thrown down from the ground from a distance medium or higher in the air. The opponent impacts the surface with all the force of an actual meteor itself, opponents being engulfed in flame before making their fiery final impact. Upon making their final fiery impact, everyone within short range of the impact immediately needs to make a balance check to avoid falling prone at a difficulty equal to (The Solar\u2019s Essence or 3, whichever is higher). Additionally everyone in the blast radius must immediately save against a special one time environmental hazard of 10i/instant with a trauma of (3 or solar\u2019s essence, whichever is higher). This damage ignores all soak and does lethal in crash. Charms such as Sledgehammer Fist Punch and its expansions may be used reflexively upon impact to increase the damage rendered on such objects with a mote discount equal to (3 or Solar\u2019s Essence, whichever is higher). This charm is powered by killing intent, thus the Lawgiver cannot throw an ally in order for cheap destruction, it has to be someone he wishes genuine harm to.<br /> <br /> <b>HORIZON HURLING TACTIC</b><br /> <b>Cost\u200b</b>: - (+10m 1WP)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 3\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: Mirror (Crack the Sky [Infernals])<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Heaven Thunder Hammer<br /> <br /> It is said that for every star in the sky there was a person who though they could get away with angering the Solar champion. This charm may be activated upon knocking out or killing an opponent while still deciding to launch them with Heaven Thunder Hammer or by performing an amount of damage equal to the opponent\u2019s (Essence + Stamina) while they are in initiative crash. If successful the entire area wrecked with a devastating sonic boom as the Solar\u2019s opponent is blasted off towards the horizon itself, launching the opponent multiple kilometers/extreme brands away so that combat is no longer feasible. Upon impact, the victim makes a medium sized impact crater in the ground and anything that requires a Strength 5 feat is automatically destroyed or blown back while the victim always takes the worst impact damage from Heaven Thunder Hammer possible, which is usually almost bashing.<br /> <br /> Quick allied travel with this charm is impossible, as this charm functions off of killing intent, yadda yadda point is you cannot use it on allies unless you actually want to beat them senseless.<br /> <br /> <b>SKY BREAKER PUNCH</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>\u200b: - (+5m 1WP)\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 5 Essence 5\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>\u200b: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms\u200b</b>: Horizon Hurling Tactic<br /> <br /> <i>Super Move Serious Series: Serious Punch</i><br /> <br /> For the most part, the Solar Hero is a picture of gentility. A friendly hero and face to all, but there are times for his wrath is so terrible that all of Creation would tremble at his power, nearly all of the clouds in Creation parting way from the intense pressure generated by this charm. This charm enhances Horizon Hurling Tactic and may only be used on an opponent in initiative crash and when the Solar makes an attack that is at least 30 or more raw decisive damage. Instead of launching the opponent miles, the distance is theoretically infinite. Meaning a Solar in Coral could launch a Realm Dragonblooded Solar clear across the West, bank him off the Imperial Mountain, before having him impact directly into his House\u2019s main building. In addition to the worse damage from a Heaven Thunder Impact as possible, people who crash into the ground due to this charm are unable to move for five days, as the force of the impact rattled their body beyond comprehension. A physical threat (such as an attack or environmental hazard), social attack, or even simply slapping the victim across the face would be enough to wake them up.<br /> <br /> There are a few conditions for this charm:<ul><li>The location must be specific, that is you cannot send an opponent infinitely sailing into space or the Wyld. You do not need a specific location as a general one is fine (EX: \u201cCrash this Dragonblooded directly in front of the Imperial Castle\u201d). \u201cAnywhere\u201d is also acceptable, in which the Storyteller decides the location.</li> <li>The location cannot be actively hidden and with you unaware of it.</li> <li>The end location cannot be autodeath of the opponent. For example, attempting to bank the First and Forsaken Lion off of the Underworld Calendar and into the maw of Oblivion to instantly kill him is not allowed unless your attack would defeat the Deathlord pre launch. If he survives, than the best you can do is land them in a place where the environment can still be very lethal, such as just above oblivion where insane ghosts will claw at the Deathlord for him to enter the Void. If Lieger is launched into Isidoros throat, he may instead avoid being swallowed at the last moment, but have to deal with Isidoros gnashing teeth and acidic saliva. This also includes such places where there is literally no possible escape from (Such as the Sun itself). This is in addition to impact damage however.</li> <li>Launching people to the moon is a valid tactic in vanilla Exalted, as there is air up there. How they will get back is another matter, as would Luna\u2019s displeasure at dealing with uninvited guests... unless it's someone she hates in which good job getting her a present.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>DOME SHATTERING SMITE</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>\u200b: -\u037e <b>Mins</b>\u200b: Brawl 2 Essence 1\u037e <b>Type</b>:\u200b Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords</b>\u200b: None<br /> <b>Duration\u200b</b>: Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite charms</b>\u200b: Fists of Iron<br /> <br /> The Exalts bare fists have the power to fell the mightiest of giants. This charm permanently upgrades the Exalts bare hands, letting them have the smashing tag.<br /> <br /> If the Exalt has Heaven Thunder Hammer and is Essence +3 then that charm is also automatically upgraded. If the Solar Hero makes a smashing attack in addition to the blow from Heaven Thunder Hammer, than the total distance one flies is increased by one range brand automatically. However the impact damage does not change. Yes this is kind of a shortcut, but I don\u2019t get why Essence +7 is a needed upgrade to make people fly out to medium range for a strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":".  fixes 12-26-2015, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:18:39-08:00","id":793265,"title":"","content":"Nice quotes. Very fitting.<br /> <br /> As for the Charms themselves...I like the last four, but the first three feel off to me somehow. Not sure exactly why.<br /> <br /> I don't think you really need the &quot;no using these for travel&quot; restrictions. If someone's willing to take a Heaven Thunder Hammer to get somewhere, I think they deserve to get there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T14:20:48-08:00","id":793267,"title":"","content":"I feel like Sky-Breaker Punch is getting to the same narrative level of Nine Aeons Thew - that is, the pinnacle of a particular concept, and the foundation for custom displays of egregious but specific power. I'd put it at E4 or E5 for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T15:12:03-08:00","id":793284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/792796-christmas-present-for-kinda-everyone-3e-solar-brawl-punch-charms?p=793267#post793267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Sky-Breaker Punch is getting to the same narrative level of Nine Aeons Thew - that is, the pinnacle of a particular concept, and the foundation for custom displays of egregious but specific power. I'd put it at E4 or E5 for that reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be ESS 5, I just copy-pasted the last charm statblock and forgot the Essence rating. Quality!Will fix now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax\">Sanctaphrax</a>[/B]]Nice quotes. Very fitting.<br /> <br /> As for the Charms themselves...I like the last four, but the first three feel off to me somehow. Not sure exactly why.<br /> <br /> I don't think you really need the &quot;no using these for travel&quot; restrictions. If someone's willing to take a Heaven Thunder Hammer to get somewhere, I think they deserve to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably because they're FoS-ish charms. Even since 2e I felt Sledgehammer should've been an athletics charm if some sort rather than native MA/brawl<br /> <br /> As for the fast travel, I may have been overzealous prehaps, but its not just punching, but you're not only going to need to beat a person badly, but also give them a punch they're most likely not going to forget (The damage needed to launch them then taking that horrific impact damage). A lot of these were warm ups for Malfeas FoS and Infernal Monster charms though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:09:18-08:00","id":1177348,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the epic thread Necro, but has I was wondering if anyone had used any of these charms in their games. If so, how did it go?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T20:13:14-08:00","id":1178321,"title":"","content":"Not that I know of ironically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T09:38:03-08:00","id":1178459,"title":"","content":"I'll have to get back to you after I've bought a few then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/513-gatts","name":"Gatts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}